    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0342" n="170" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg170"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857/399</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Swansea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Moorhead</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Swansea</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-03-10">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 10, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 8.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Affidavits John Ripp, American citizen, cook, and of chief
                    officer, British bark <hi rendition="#italic">Inverlogie</hi>, bound from
                    Cardiff, cargo coal, for Russia; stopped by German submarine Bristol Channel by
                    warning shot over vessel, no attack made until crew clear of vessel, bark then
                    sunk, ho attempt to escape made. Heavy sea running time of attack, lifeboats
                    kept afloat with difficulty, submarine gave <pb facs="0343" n="171"
                        xml:id="pg171"/> no assistance. No casualties, crew in mate’s boat rescued
                    after seven hours by French steamer, landed Swansea; crew captain’s boat rescued
                    by schooner, destination unknown. Department [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Embassy?</hi>] informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moorhead</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
